From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TinyYana <yanasakuranight@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 18:29:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] do not let a gateway exit adjustment overwrite a redirected
 teleport

TheEndGatewayBlockEntity#teleportRegionThreading has two branches. The exact one
teleports blind. The inexact one teleports to the raw exit portal position first
and then, in the placement callback, moves the entity again to
findExitPosition(...) - because on this platform the exit chunk cannot be read
before the teleport.

That second move is unconditional, and it runs after the teleport event this fork
restores. So in the inexact branch a handler's setTo is silently undone, while in
the exact branch it is honoured: the two branches disagree. On Paper there is no
disagreement, because getPortalDestination resolves the exit before the event and
the handler always has the last word.

Adjust only when the entity is where this teleport asked it to be. The check is
exact rather than approximate: the transition carries an absolute position and
the callback runs at placement, before anything can have moved it. It also stops
the adjustment from reading the gateway world's blocks from whatever region a
redirect landed in, which would be an ownership violation rather than a
behavioural difference.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/level/block/entity/TheEndGatewayBlockEntity.java b/net/minecraft/world/level/block/entity/TheEndGatewayBlockEntity.java
index fdf220424f7693a7ea3ae385ddd771720825b0f7..d05a86e3ced1b64d87371744b5abbe3687cf5e3b 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/level/block/entity/TheEndGatewayBlockEntity.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/level/block/entity/TheEndGatewayBlockEntity.java
@@ -224,9 +224,27 @@ public class TheEndGatewayBlockEntity extends TheEndPortalBlockEntity {
             // should be teleported, something something else...
             // however, we know the target location cannot differ by one region section: so we can
             // just teleport and adjust the position after
+            final Vec3 requestedExit = teleport.position(); // Lecithin - see below
             return toTeleport.teleportAsync(
                 teleport, net.minecraft.world.entity.Entity.TELEPORT_FLAG_LOAD_CHUNK | net.minecraft.world.entity.Entity.TELEPORT_FLAG_TELEPORT_PASSENGERS,
                 (net.minecraft.world.entity.Entity teleportedEntity) -> {
+                    // Lecithin start - do not overwrite a destination a teleport event redirected.
+                    // On Paper the exit position is resolved inside getPortalDestination, so the
+                    // teleport event already carries the adjusted position and a handler's setTo is
+                    // the last word. Here the platform teleports to the raw exit first and adjusts
+                    // afterwards, so an unconditional adjust would silently undo setTo - and would
+                    // read portalWorld's blocks from whatever region the redirect landed in. Both
+                    // are avoided by adjusting only when the entity is where this teleport asked it
+                    // to be, which is exact: the transition carries an absolute position and this
+                    // callback runs at placement, before anything can have moved it.
+                    if (teleportedEntity.level() != portalWorld
+                        || teleportedEntity.position().distanceToSqr(requestedExit) > 1.0E-6) {
+                        if (post != null) {
+                            post.onTransition(teleportedEntity);
+                        }
+                        return;
+                    }
+                    // Lecithin end
                     // adjust to the final exit position
                     Vec3 adjusted = Vec3.atCenterOf(TheEndGatewayBlockEntity.findExitPosition(portalWorld, teleportPos));
                     // teleportTo will adjust rider positions
